## Guards — what we PREVENT (the twin of detection)

A guard is **not a separate object from a contract — it is the enforcement of one**, so it lives
here, never in a second register. **Register the TEETH** — the `Blocks / flags` cell is the
difference between a gate and a poster, and it is invisible from the code's tone. **Register the
DEFECT too**: a rule enforced by hand-copied snippets with no module of record gets the honest
cell *"no module of record"* — a register whose rows all look healthy is a register nobody fixes.

| Guard (what it prevents) | Level | Blocks / flags | Owner | Source (index, not copy) |
|---|---|---|---|---|

